      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#19745 (\"Fix none-comparison (E711) warnings\") was merged in March and cleaned up `== None` / `!= None` comparisons across the repo, including one line in `rpd_utils.py`:\n\n```python\n# before #19745\nif min_time == None:\n    raise Exception(\"Trace file is empty.\")\n# after\nif min_time is None:\n```\n\nThat PR missed three more in the same function, `rpd_to_chrome_trace`: the `start != None` conditions in the `rangeStringApi` / `rangeStringOp` / `rangeStringMonitor` assignments, in the end-time branch of the range filter builder.\n\nThis PR fixes those three lines with the exact same change `#19745` applied to the line next to them. After this, `python/sglang/` is fully clean under `ruff check --select=E711` — these are the last hits.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`python/sglang/srt/utils/rpd_utils.py`: three lines, `start != None` becomes `start is not None`.\n\n`start` is either None or a string from argparse (possibly with a `%` suffix for relative time). `!=` and `is not None` agree on every reachable value, so no behavior change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model output changes; profiler tooling only. Verified locally:\n\n- `ruff check --select=E711 python/sglang/` passes after the change\n- `ruff check --select=F401,F821,F823,UP037` and `ruff format --check` pass on the file\n- module imports cleanly\n\nNo unit test added: one-line None-comparison fix, #19745 shipped without tests for the same change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable, three comparison operators in a one-shot CLI tool.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (out of scope for a comparison fix, same as #19745)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to the [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (nothing to document)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to the [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (not applicable)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidelines](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39939987857](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39939987857)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39939987842](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39939987842)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39939987701](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39939987701)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
